<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Wilhelm, Duke of Saxe-Eisenach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1666">1666</a>–<a href="/years/1729">1729</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as John William of Saxe-Eisenach</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Wilhelm, Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenach">Eisenach</a>, ruled the small Ernestine duchy from 1698 to 1729. His court at Eisenach kept a notable musical establishment, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georg-philipp-telemann">Georg Philipp Telemann</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapellmeister">Kapellmeister</a>, in the town where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-sebastian-bach">Johann Sebastian Bach</a> was born. His line died out with his son William Henry in 1741, after which Eisenach passed to Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-wilhelm-duke-of-saxe-eisenach.jpg" alt="Johann Wilhelm, Duke of Saxe-Eisenach" width="320" height="473" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Peter Feuerlein · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Feuerlein_-_Duke_Johann_Wilhelm_of_Saxony-Eisenach.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
